<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John of Austria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1547–1578</span> · Also known as Don John of Austria, Don Juan de Austria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> was an illegitimate son of the Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>, recognised by his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a>. He suppressed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moriscos">Morisco</a> revolt of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alpujarras">Alpujarras</a> in 1568–1571 and commanded the fleet of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-league-1571">Holy League</a> that defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> at Lepanto in 1571. In 1573 he recaptured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>, and he died in 1578 as governor-general of the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-of-austria.jpg" alt="John of Austria" width="320" height="614" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Don_Juan_d%27Austria_1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
